{
    "Description": {
        "Id": "event_co_BageleMech_R3",
        "Name": "Bagele's Ride",
        "Details": "The priority transmission indicator flashes on your command console aboard the <i>Argo</i>.\r\n\r\nDarius glances at the source identifier and immediately closes his eyes. \"Commander. Before I answer this, I want it officially recorded that I know exactly who this is.\"\r\n\r\nYou sigh.\r\n\r\n \"Put it through.\"\r\n\r\nThe pirate appears on screen. This time he looks exhausted. The camera feed shakes slightly as he adjusts it, revealing the customized Hatchetman behind him. Or rather, what remains assembled of it. Several access panels are missing. One arm hangs suspended from a maintenance gantry. The cockpit canopy sits on a workbench in the background. Various components have been tagged, inventoried, and chained down. Most concerning of all, several pirates can be seen lurking suspiciously close to the BattleMech while attempting to look innocent.\r\n\r\n \"Commander! Just the person I wanted to see.\"\r\n\r\nA loud metallic clanging sound echoes from somewhere off camera. The pirate leader immediately turns his head. \"Put that HeatSink back where you found it!\"\r\n\r\nA muffled voice responds.\r\n\r\n <i>\"I was cleaning it!\"</i>\r\n\r\n \"You were carrying it toward your personal shuttle!\" The pirate turns back toward the camera and forces a smile. \"Crew management. The true challenge of leadership.\"\r\n\r\nAt the mention of the BattleMech, Bagele practically materializes beside your command station. His eyes widen in horror. \"What happened to my Hatchetman?!\"\r\n\r\n\"Preventative maintenance,\" the pirate replies quickly. Another loud crash sounds from off screen. \"THAT POLLY IS NOT A SOUVENIR!\" the pirate roars. Several figures immediately scatter out of view. The pirate rubs his temples.\r\n\r\n \"Commander, do you have any idea how difficult it is to stop pirates from stealing parts off a BattleMech that technically belongs to somebody else?\"\r\n\r\n\"Apparently very difficult,\" Darius mutters.\r\n\r\n\"Extremely difficult.\" The pirate sighs heavily. \"Every day I keep this machine intact costs me money, personnel, and increasingly creative explanations.\"\r\n\r\nBagele looks physically distressed. \"It's still all there, right?\"\r\n\r\n \"Mostly.\" the pirate shrugs.\r\n\r\nBagele's face falls.\r\n\r\n\"Mostly?\"\r\n\r\n\"Everything important is still there,\" the pirate says quickly. \"Anything missing has been recovered. Probably.\" He points toward the camera. \"Which brings us back to the reason for this call. The current storage and maintenance fee remains three million C-Bills. Against all business sense and repeated recommendations from my associates.\" One of the pirates in the background shouts, <i>\"Can I have the targeting computer if they say no?\"</i>\r\n\r\n\"NO!\" both the pirate leader and Bagele shout simultaneously. The pirate sighs.\r\n\r\n \"Commander. Before somebody successfully steals an entire limb, what's it going to be?\"",
