                        "Name": "Not Interested.",
                        "Details": "You don't hesitate. \"No.\"\r\n\r\n The pirate blinks. \"No?\"\r\n\r\n \"No. Three million C-Bills for a salvaged Hatchetman is absurd.\"\r\n\r\n The pirate looks genuinely disappointed. \"A shame. I was beginning to enjoy these conversations.\"\r\n\r\n Bagele's face falls. \"Commander...\"\r\n\r\n You shake your head. \"The answer is final.\"\r\n\r\n The pirate sighs dramatically. \"A tragedy.\"\r\n\r\n \"No,\" you reply. \"A business decision.\"\r\n\r\n The pirate nods reluctantly. \"Fair enough. Can't fault a commander for knowing where the line is.\"\r\n\r\n Bagele looks away from the screen, unable to hide his disappointment. The pirate notices. \"Sorry, friend. Looks like your reunion wasn't meant to be.\"\r\n\r\n The transmission terminates. The screen goes dark. Silence hangs over the command deck.\r\n\r\n Bagele stares at the blank display for several moments before finally speaking. \"...Understood, Commander.\"\r\n\r\n The words are professional. The disappointment behind them isn't.",
